🎤 1-Minute Perfect Intro (DevOps Engineer)
“I’m a DevOps Engineer with around 4 years of experience working on AWS and modern DevOps tools. My primary focus is on building reliable and scalable systems and automating the software delivery lifecycle.

In my current role, I design and manage CI/CD pipelines using Jenkins, where I automate build, test, and deployment processes. I also use Terraform for Infrastructure as Code to provision and manage cloud resources like EC2, VPC, and EKS, ensuring consistency across environments.

I actively work on monitoring and observability using tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and CloudWatch to track system health and quickly identify issues. I’ve also handled production incidents where I troubleshoot failures, restore services, and implement preventive measures.

Additionally, I focus on optimizing performance and reducing cloud costs through auto-scaling and right-sizing strategies. I collaborate closely with development and QA teams to ensure smooth and faster releases. Overall, my goal is to improve system reliability, automate processes, and enable efficient delivery.”

🔥 Real Project Example (Very High Impact Answer)
“In my current project, we have a microservices-based application deployed on AWS using Kubernetes (EKS). My responsibility was to build a complete CI/CD pipeline and ensure production reliability.

I implemented Jenkins pipelines that automatically trigger on code commits, run tests, build Docker images, and deploy them to Kubernetes using Helm. This reduced deployment time significantly and eliminated manual errors.

For infrastructure, I used Terraform with an S3 remote backend and DynamoDB locking to manage environments like dev, staging, and production. This improved consistency and team collaboration.

On the operations side, I set up monitoring using Prometheus and Grafana dashboards, along with alerting for critical metrics like CPU, memory, and latency. During a production issue where latency spiked, I analyzed metrics and logs, identified a resource bottleneck, and resolved it by tuning autoscaling policies.

I also worked on cost optimization by identifying underutilized resources and implementing auto-scaling, which reduced cloud costs noticeably. This project helped improve system reliability, deployment speed, and overall efficiency.”
